WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.902
-Thank you very much for
watching "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.104
everybody. I appreciate it.
I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.273
Let's get to the news and jokes.
Well, guys.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.776
Bob Woodward has a new book
coming out about the President,

00:00:10.776 --> 00:00:13.412
and one story is making
major headlines today.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:16.950
It turns out Trump knew
way back in early February

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.918
how bad the coronavirus was,

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.487
but he continued to downplay it
to the American people.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.389
And Woodward's
got it all on tape

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:25.725
because Trump let him
record their conversations.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.961
Check this out.
Here's Trump in mid-March.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.304
Yeah. I remember Americans
not panicking when they spent

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:41.840
thousands for a roll
of toilet paper on eBay.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.776
Seriously. You didn't
want to create a panic?

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.078
For the last six months,

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:47.747
I've been opening doorknobs
with my knees.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.150
How could he downplay this?

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.585
He's treated the pandemic

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.520
like those flash-flood alerts
on your phone.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.690
Like, "Eh.
I'm sure it's nothing.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.159
Never heard this phone
make that sound before, though."

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:02.395
Yeah, it's a catastrophic
story for Trump

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.397
that threatens
to end his presidency,

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:08.201
or, as he calls it, Wednesday.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.836
These tapes are insane.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.438
Here's Trump talking about
the virus in early February.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:14.707
Listen to this.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.696
Up until then, Trump thought

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:39.499
"deadly stuff"
was a brand of Oreos.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.204
Meanwhile, Trump heard
the recording and was like,

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:46.772
"I never met that guy.
I don't know who he is."

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:49.075
Seriously,
these tapes are really bad.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.476
Trump's reelection prospects

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:55.481
are sinking faster
than a boat at a MAGA rally.

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.383
I don't know.
Maybe I'm being too critical.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.752
Before I pass judgment,
I should read the other

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.956
40 Trump books
that came out this week.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.691
And despite Trump saying
as recently as last month

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:07.860
that kids are almost immune
from the virus,

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.962
it turns out he knew
that wasn't the truth

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:12.699
all the way back in March.
Check out this clip.

00:02:24.042 --> 00:02:25.378
I'd say at this point

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.281
the dude needs to give HIMSELF
some hush money.

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:30.549
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:31.951
Is he serious?

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.621
He knew all that and still
fought for schools to reopen?

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:39.025
Even Vladimir Putin was like,
"Not cool, dude. Not cool."

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:42.494
Now, despite what the numerous
tell-all books say about him,

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:45.164
Trump received a pretty
surprising nomination today.

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:46.899
-President Trump
has been nominated

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.268
for the 2021 Nobel Peace Prize.

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:52.404
Here's how --
a far-right Norwegian lawmaker

00:02:52.404 --> 00:02:54.740
is telling news outlets he
submitted the President's name

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.342
to the committee
for the President's work

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.911
on that agreement
between Israel and the UAE.

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:01.380
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.449
-In response, Trump was like,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:06.952
"How do you say 'vote twice'
in Norwegian?"

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:10.756
"Vottka-tuug."

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:13.126
Yeah, Trump thinks
he's getting the Peace Prize

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:17.496
for uniting Americans
and the coronavirus.

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:19.865
Meanwhile, Trump is focused
on the upcoming election,

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:21.901
and last night,
he delivered a campaign speech

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.836
in North Carolina.
At one point,

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.171
he mentioned Kamala Harris,

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.173
and here's what
he had to say about her.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.642
-You know what?
People don't like her.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:32.945
Nobody likes her.

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:36.649
She could never be
the first woman president.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.384
She could never be.
[ Crowd jeering ]

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.487
That would be an insult
to our country.

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:43.222
-Mike Pence was like,
"Hey, cool it, man.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.491
Some of us has to
debate her next month."

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:48.961
I wonder what Trump thinks is so
insulting about Kamala Harris.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.297
I feel like the answer
is white in front of me.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.799
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.667
[ Rim shot ]

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.203
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.203 --> 00:04:00.439
♪♪

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:02.175
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.644
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.380
Trump was like,
"She's so unpopular,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:11.016
her approval rating is barely
20 points higher than mine."

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:13.219
Later on in his speech,
Trump mentioned something

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:14.887
he used to talk about
all the time.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.122
Check it out.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:18.057
-And you know
Mexico is paying for the wall,

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.458
just so you understand,

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:21.627
but we're going to charge them
a small fee at the border.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.462
You know, the toll booths.
We have toll booths.

00:04:23.462 --> 00:04:26.699
And we're gonna get all the
money that we spent on the wall

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.100
will be coming back.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.137
So, remember I used to say,
"Who's going to pay for it?"

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.806
They'd say, "Mexico."
That's right.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:37.509
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:39.811
-And then Trump announced
a new branch of the military,

00:04:39.811 --> 00:04:42.748
the Toll Booth Force.

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:44.283
They all would say --
They always would say that.

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:46.118
I would say, "Who's gonna --"
They said, "Who's gonna pay?"

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:48.721
And they all would say.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.956
That sounds like
an interesting idea.

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:53.091
Our borders will be protected
by a giant wall

00:04:53.091 --> 00:04:55.261
and that little toll-booth arm
that goes up and down.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.462
No problem.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.097
Here's some big
entertainment news

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.599
that caught a lot of people
by surprise. Listen to this.

00:05:00.599 --> 00:05:03.903
-Season 20 of "Keeping Up
with the Kardashians"

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:05.504
will be its last.

00:05:05.504 --> 00:05:08.106
The show has run on E!
for the past 14 years,

00:05:08.106 --> 00:05:11.611
following Kim, Khloé, Kourtney,
Kris, and the whole crew

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.579
as they went about
their daily lives.

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.615
-Wow.
It's a tough blow for fans

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:18.017
who will now only be able
to keep up with the family

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.286
through Instagram,
TikTok, Twitter, tabloids,

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:21.920
and the Internet.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.790
Right now all the executives
at the E! Network are like,

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:30.262
"So...how are we gonna fill
20 hours a day?"

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:32.731
Well, guys, as if these
aren't scary enough times,

00:05:32.731 --> 00:05:35.468
listen to what happened
earlier today in New Jersey.

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:40.006
-The magnitude-3.1 earthquake
reported in New Jersey.

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:42.442
According to the
U.S. Geological Survey,

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:44.677
it was centered
near East Freehold.

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.079
-That's right. There was an
earthquake in New Jersey.

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:50.249
It was crazy. There were
track suits thrown everywhere.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:53.686
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:57.656
The entire state
looked like every TJ Maxx.

00:05:57.656 --> 00:05:59.591
It was a pretty decent
earthquake.

00:05:59.591 --> 00:06:06.265
Scientists in Jersey
gave it 3 out of 10 "Ohhhhh's!"

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:08.066
Well, here's some
interesting news.

00:06:08.066 --> 00:06:11.037
The U.S. Air Force is testing
out a new kind of technology --

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:12.404
robot dogs.

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:14.373
Check this out.

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:15.941
[ Menacing music plays ]

00:06:15.941 --> 00:06:19.912
♪♪

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:22.715
I hope the robot dogs work,
otherwise, we're going to be

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:25.818
seeing a lot of Sarah McLachlan
robot-dog commercials.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:28.354
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.925
And finally, a man in Illinois

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:36.295
celebrated his 100th birthday
in an exciting way.

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:37.463
Watch this.

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:40.065
-An Illinois man
celebrating his 100th birthday

00:06:40.065 --> 00:06:42.668
by breaking a wet and wild
world record.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:45.705
Bill Lambert became
the world's oldest scuba diver

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:47.807
by taking a plunge
in Pearl Lake.

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:50.276
He says his goal
is to stay in shape

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:54.079
and break it again
when he turns 101.

00:06:54.079 --> 00:06:55.581
-Actually, it wasn't
that hard for him.

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:58.184
He's been carrying around
an oxygen tank for years.

00:06:58.184 --> 00:07:01.086
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:04.256
It was an unforgettable day
for him...and also the deck hand

00:07:04.256 --> 00:07:07.026
who had to help him
into his wet suit.

